1537:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *
1538:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** * Summary:
1539:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  Sets one of up to four ADC configurations. Before setting the new
1540:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  configuration, the ADC is stopped and powered down. After setting
1541:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  the new configuration, the ADC can be powered and conversion
1542:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  can be restarted depending up on the value of second parameter
1543:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  restart. If the value of this parameter is 1, then ADC will be
1544:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  restarted. If this value is zero, then user must call ADC_DelSig_1_Start
1545:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  and ADC_DelSig_1_StartConvert() to restart the conversion.
1546:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *
1547:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** * Parameters:
1548:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  config:  configuration user wants to select.
1549:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *           Valid range: 1..4
1550:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  restart:  Restart option. 1 means start the ADC and restart the conversion.
1551:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *                            0 means do not start the ADC and conversion.
1552:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *
1553:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** * Return:
1554:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  None
1555:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *
1556:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** * Side Effects: 
1557:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *  Enables internal interrupt.
1558:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *
1559:Generated_Source\PSoC5/ADC_DelSig_1.c **** *******************************************************************************/
